        "a": "Almost certainly because the data moved, not because your code did. Wearable days get retro-edited when a device syncs late, sleep gets re-staged hours after the fact, and a second device joining the account starts contributing overlapping intervals. Any assertion on a live account's values has a shelf life of days. Assert on values only against fixtures you control, and use the real account only to check that the fixtures still resemble the provider."
