        "a": "Ugly days and rude faults. Two overlapping sleep segments from two devices, a day retro-edited between two reads, a night crossing a DST transition, a mid-day gap, a device clock two minutes off. On the fault side: a 429 with no Retry-After header at all, since RFC 6585 makes that header a MAY rather than a MUST, a Retry-After expressed as an HTTP-date rather than seconds, a truncated body, and an HTML error page from a CDN instead of JSON. A vendor sandbox is built to demonstrate the happy path; your fake exists to attack it."
